  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, there is zero evidence about which design choices matter. The most informative first experiment is a clean, minimal baseline that anchors the configuration space. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest RNA-only configuration using the most standard encoder (PCA) and the simplest profile setting. It establishes a reference performance level for the RNA modality, confirms the pipeline runs correctly, and provides a baseline against which all other modalities (image-only, multimodal) and more complex encoders (scvi, scgpt) can be compared. Under a limited budget, starting with the lowest-risk, most interpretable baseline reduces the risk of a failed first run and gives a clear anchor for subsequent exploration of image modality, multimodal fusion, and advanced encoders."
}

